 the speed  it was come coming at us and it was just  a case of fighting for our lives getting  to getting to the roof  they never saw their parents again the  parents sacrificed themselves to get our  youngest brother sister out of their  room and then they went their separate  ways and that's kind of yeah what  happened that Robert and Paul spent  hours searching for their family they  found their younger brother first and  finally at the end of the day they found  their little sister both had been pushed  up trees by their parents before they  themselves were washed away through the  chaos of the devastated country  the boys hitchhiked with a younger  siblings almost a hundred miles back to  Colombo quite lucky that we were brought  up like that soon we've said the other  day that if the tsunami happened to us  when we were just on a two-week holiday  we wouldn't have been as tough and we  wouldn't have doubted it how we have but  because we was traveling around and we  always saw people a lot worse off than  what we we were it kind of made it  easier to deal with  three years ago inspired by their  parents entrepreneurial spirit the  brothers set up their flip-flop business  which sprang from their love of  traveling we instantly knew this was the  perfect way of creating something  sustainable in which we could build a  brand based on our beliefs and this is  why we introduced orphans for orphans  the success of the brand boosts their  charity the Gandhi foundation which  raises money for children in India and  Sri Lanka that was like young shangkun  children we met that helps us get home  or you know helps us on the day you kind  of just grateful that those kind of  people showed just the the greatest side  of human nature honored on a day of  desperate need  see you then kind of feel yourself going  with they helped us in our hour of need  so you then want to want to help them  and this Christmas they're seeing the  concrete results as their first  orphanage 